# Example of the local Supabase CLI secrets file.
#
# Copy this to `supabase/.env` (gitignored) and fill in the real value, then
# run `supabase stop && supabase start` to apply.
#
# This file is read by the SUPABASE CLI (for env() substitution in
# config.toml) — NOT by the Next.js app and NOT by Vercel. The Google client
# secret is a Supabase-side credential: on prod it lives in the Supabase
# dashboard (Auth > Providers > Google); locally it lives here. Your deployed
# app never reads it, so it does NOT belong in Vercel env.

# Google OAuth client secret (from your Google Cloud "Web application" client).
SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_SECRET=
